id: pm-rusbe4
title: "GH-870: make runtime workspace path assertions portable in Windows nightly"
description: "The scheduled Windows Node 24 leg fails after 6,686 passing tests because runtime-extended-actions asserts a POSIX separator fragment against a native Windows tracker root. Assert path semantics with platform-native construction so the nightly reports product behavior rather than harness spelling."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:testing",ci,github-report,portability,windows
created_at: "2026-08-02T10:36:31.773Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-02T12:22:33.136Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-02T12:22:07.217Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-02T12:22:07.217Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: The runtime extended-actions workspace snapshot assertion is separator-independent; focused coverage passes locally; a GitHub Windows Node 24 run proves the regression fixed; GitHub #870 links this canonical item
parent: pm-j668gl
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "Runtime and evidence lookup path assertions pass with native absolute paths on Windows, macOS, and Linux"
actual_result: "Implemented, regression-covered, manually package-tested, and verified on exact-head cross-platform nightly run 30747290823"
fixed_version: next-auto-release
