comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-02T10:36:31.773Z","harness:codex","created_at=now,text=Duplicate check evidence: searched every status for Windows nightly, runtime extended actions, workspace snapshot paths, and separator assertions. pm-j668gl is the broad portability parent and historical items cover different failures; no existing item owns GitHub #870. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/870."
  "2026-08-02T10:38:31.655Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: workspace snapshot adapter assertion now uses path.join, preserving the same semantic suffix on POSIX and Windows. Focused runtime adapter suite passes; hosted Windows proof remains a PR gate."
  "2026-08-02T11:28:22.485Z","harness:codex","Repository-wide verification: 418 test files and 6,703 tests passed under the sandboxed coverage runner with exact 100% statements (47,529/47,529), branches (34,246/34,246), functions (9,673/9,673), and lines (46,119/46,119). No coverage thresholds, exclusions, or ignore counts were weakened."
  "2026-08-02T11:35:49.109Z","harness:codex","Packed-consumer acceptance: pnpm smoke:npx passed the generated tarball across 15 packaged modules. An independent tarball was then installed from unrelated root /tmp/tmp.0PKR29g4Dz into separate npm and Bun consumers with isolated project/global trackers; both initialized, created items, added evidence, and returned files lookup total=1. npm additionally proved atomic files/docs replacement and exact repeated evidence changed=false."
  "2026-08-02T11:54:03.187Z","harness:codex","Hosted matrix evidence: run 30746262926 passed Ubuntu Node 22/24/25 and macOS Node 24. Windows Node 24 passed build/typecheck and 6,697 tests but failed the new SDK absolute-path reverse-lookup case (total 0 vs 1). The original GH-870 separator assertion passed; this additional Windows-only canonicalization defect is now part of the active portability correction before completion."
  "2026-08-02T12:00:18.591Z","harness:codex","Correction verification: canonical workspace and requested absolute paths are now resolved through filesystem identity before relative projection. Focused context-management and runtime Windows suites passed 14/14; typecheck, lint, zero-clone duplication, static/docstring/package/SDK/token/context gates passed; full coverage passed 418 files and 6,703 tests at exact 100/100/100/100. Hosted rerun remains the acceptance gate."
  "2026-08-02T12:10:46.777Z","harness:codex","Hosted rerun 30746914306 proved the canonicalized project-absolute lookup now passes on Windows. Its sole remaining failure moved to the following global-scope assertion: the fixture hard-coded POSIX /tmp as an absolute path, which Windows correctly treats as relative. Replaced that fixture with path.join(os.tmpdir(), filename) so every OS exercises a genuinely external absolute path."
  "2026-08-02T12:21:52.566Z","harness:codex","Hosted acceptance: exact head fd69b84335ead8ef1022b606a470166e78c9f188 passed nightly run 30747290823 on Windows Node 24, macOS Node 24, and Ubuntu Node 22/24/25. Ubuntu Node 24 also passed secret scan, exact 100% coverage, static quality, and compatibility migration gates."
